# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository stores LF in every blob already; this file makes the WORKING
# TREE agree on every platform. Without it, Windows checkouts honour
# `core.autocrlf=true` and land CRLF on disk, while Linux checkouts land LF.
#
# That split is invisible to git — `git status` is clean either way, because
# the blobs are identical — but it is not invisible to Prettier, whose
# `endOfLine` default is "lf". On this Windows machine `pnpm format:check`
# reported 800 of 1050 tracked files as unformatted, every one of them a false
# positive about a byte the repository does not contain. A gate that fails for
# 800 files nobody touched is a gate people learn to ignore, and it hides the
# handful of real formatting errors underneath.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf per-repository, so contributors need no
# local git configuration and CI needs no change. Normalising costs no diff:
# the blobs are LF today and stay byte-identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be EOL-converted. `text=auto` already detects most of
# these, but detection is a heuristic and a corrupted PNG is an expensive way
# to discover its limits.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.avif   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.node   binary
*.dll    binary
*.exe    binary

# Generated and vendored trees: keep them out of language statistics and out
# of diffs, without changing how they are stored.
pnpm-lock.yaml            linguist-generated=true -diff
packages/database/generated/** linguist-generated=true -diff
